        "id": "story",
        "type": "story",
        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "Rain or shine"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Arun said, \"We will play outside, but if it rains we will stay in. Hurrah! The sun is out!\"\n\"Notice the joining words and the cry of joy,\" said the teacher."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "conjunction",
          "determiner",
          "interjection"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "A conjunction joins words or sentences: and, but, or, because, although. She was tired but she kept walking.\nA determiner comes before a noun: a, an, the, this, that, some, many, my. It tells which or how many.\nAn interjection shows sudden feeling: Hurrah! Oh! Wow! It is followed by an exclamation mark."
        }
      },
